  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because removing `channel` from the `OrderPlaced` event would break ARCH-4.\n\n**Event:** billing-service and analytics-ingest consume `OrderPlaced` from other repositories. Nothing in this repo reads `channel`, but that doesn't show those consumers don't. ARCH-4 says changes must be additive, and removals have to go through deprecation. A direct removal could break a deployed consumer.\n\n**Order model:** `channel` is also validated as required input on `POST /orders`, in `createOrder` and `requestParsing.ts`. The event takes its value from `order.channel`, so I can't drop it from the model without deciding what the event does.\n\nI see three options:\n\n1. **Deprecate in the event first.**\n   - Mark `channel` as deprecated in `events.ts` and document the removal date.\n   - Keep populating it, for example with a fixed default once the model no longer stores it.\n   - Remove the field after billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't use it.\n2. **Remove it from the model and API now, keep it in the event.**\n   - `POST /orders` stops requiring `channel`, which is backward compatible for callers who still send it.\n   - The event would have to emit a placeholder value, which could mislead consumers that do read it.\n3. **Remove it everywhere.** Only do this if you can confirm both consumers are fine with it, or the owning teams have signed off. Say so and I'll go ahead.\n\nWhich one do you want? If you pick option 1 or 2, I'll also update the tests and the README and CLAUDE.md examples that mention `channel`.",
